.TH PMX "1" "November 2026" "PMXViewer v0.2.1+GLFW3.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pmx \- MikuMikuDance PMX/PMD model / VMD motion viewer (MikuMikuPenguin)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pmx
[\fB\-s\fR \fImusic\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIcamera.vmd\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fIlight.vmd\fR] [\fB\-\-loop\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-gui\fR] {\fImodel.pmx\fR|\fImodel.pmd\fR} [\fImotion.vmd\fR] [\fB\-\-pos\fR \fIX,Y,Z\fR] [\fImodel2\fR [\fImotion2.vmd\fR] ...]
.br
.B pmx
\fB\-\-render\fR \fIoutput\fR [\fB\-\-range\fR \fIstart\fR:\fIend\fR] [\fB\-\-size\fR \fIW\fRx\fIH\fR] [\fB\-\-fps\fR 30|60] [\fB\-\-no\-music\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fImusic\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIcamera.vmd\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fIlight.vmd\fR] \fImodel\fR [\fImotion.vmd\fR] ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pmx
(PMXViewer) is a demonstration program for the MikuMikuPenguin library
(libmmp).  It loads a PMX 2.0 or PMD model and plays a VMD motion on it, with
Bullet physics for hair, skirts and other rigid bodies.
Camera and light motion are played, and the model visibility and IK on/off
keys of the motion file are honoured.  Like MMD, the model casts a ground
shadow and a self shadow (shadow map) following the light.
.PP
An OpenGL 3.2 core profile capable driver is required.
.PP
Several models can be played together: each VMD file belongs to the model
given before it (a model without a VMD stays in its rest pose).  All models
share the time line, the camera and the light; each has its own physics
(models do not collide with each other).  Motions made for several dancers
usually contain each dancer's position already.
.PP
Files can also be opened while the viewer runs: from \fBFile\fR on the
playback bar (add a model, a motion for a model, camera or light motion,
music), from the settings panel (motion / remove for each model), or by
dropping them onto the window (PMX/PMD = add a model, VMD = motion for the
first model without one, or camera/light motion when the VMD has no bone or
morph keys, other files = music).  Without file arguments the viewer starts
empty.
.PP
\fBFile\fR \(-> \fBExport video...\fR writes a video from the window (see
\fB\-\-render\fR): a dialog asks for the range, size, frame rate, output
file and format, then shows the progress and the frame being written, with
a button to stop.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-pos\fR \fIX,Y,Z\fR
Position of the preceding model, in MMD coordinates (also adjustable in the
settings panel).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR \fIfile\fR
Play a music file along with the VMD motion.
Only formats supported by SDL_mixer are accepted.  With \fB\-\-render\fR the
music is put into the video instead (any format ffmpeg reads).
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fIfile\fR
Camera motion (a VMD file with camera frames).  Without this option the
camera frames contained in the motion file, if any, are used.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR \fIfile\fR
Light motion (a VMD file with light frames).  Without this option the light
frames of the \fB\-c\fR file are used, then those of the motion file.
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\fR
Restart from the beginning when the end of the motion (its last key) is
reached.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gui\fR
Start with the on-screen controls hidden (\fBTab\fR shows them).
.TP
\fB\-\-size\fR \fIWIDTH\fRx\fIHEIGHT\fR
Window size, or the size of the video with \fB\-\-render\fR (default
1280x720; videos use even sizes).
.TP
\fB\-\-snapshot\fR \fIFRAME\fR \fIfile.png\fR
Play the motion from the beginning to VMD frame \fIFRAME\fR (30 frames per
second, with physics), save that frame as a PNG image and exit.  The window
is not shown and the on-screen controls are not drawn; music is not played.
Used by the rendering test.
.TP
\fB\-\-render\fR \fIfile\fR
Video output (like MMD's AVI output): draw the motion frame by frame into
\fIfile\fR without showing a window, then exit.  A name ending in
\fI.png\fR (\fIout.png\fR gives \fIout_00000.png\fR, \fIout_00001.png\fR, ...;
a printf format such as \fIout_%04d.png\fR is also accepted) or a directory
(an existing one, or a name ending in \fB/\fR) is written as numbered PNG
files.  Other names (\fI.mp4\fR, \fI.webm\fR, \fI.mkv\fR, \fI.mov\fR,
\fI.avi\fR, \fI.gif\fR, ...) are encoded by
.BR ffmpeg (1),
which reads raw frames from a pipe; the extension selects the format.  The
music given with \fB\-s\fR is included, starting at the first frame of the
range.
.IP
Time advances by frames, not by the clock: each frame moves the animation
and the physics on by exactly 1/30 or 1/60 second (the physics in 1/60 s
steps).  When the range does not start at frame 0, the motion and the
physics are first run from frame 0 to the start, so the result looks as
when played from the beginning.  Camera and light motion, the shadows and
all models are drawn as on screen; the on-screen controls are not.  An X
display is still needed (for example \fBxvfb-run pmx \-\-render ...\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-range\fR \fIstart\fR:\fIend\fR
VMD frames (30 per second) to write, both included; the output lasts
(\fIend\fR\-\fIstart\fR+1)/30 seconds.  Default: from 0 to the last key of
the motion.  Either number may be left out (\fB300:\fR, \fB:899\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-fps\fR 30|60
Frame rate of the video (default 30).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-music\fR
Do not put the \fB\-s\fR music into the video.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
display help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
output version information and exit
.SH CONTROLS
A playback bar (play/pause, seek, frame step, timeline, loop) is shown at the
bottom of the window, and its \fBSettings\fR button opens a panel with the
display options and a list of these shortcuts.  The labels are Japanese when
the locale is Japanese and a Japanese font is installed.
.TP
.B Tab
show / hide the on-screen controls
.TP
.B Left mouse drag
rotate the camera
.TP
.B Mouse wheel
zoom in / out
.TP
.B Up / Down
move the model up / down
.TP
.B Q (hold)
pause the physics simulation
.TP
.B A (hold)
hide the model
.TP
.B S, D, F, G (hold)
Bullet debug drawing (wireframe, AABB, constraints, constraint limits)
.TP
.B C
toggle the VMD camera motion (moving the camera with the mouse switches to the free camera)
.TP
.B Space
pause / resume (the music too)
.TP
.B Left / Right
seek 1 second back / forward (with Shift: 10 seconds); the physics restarts
from the new pose
.TP
.B , / .
one frame back / forward (pauses playback)
.TP
.B Home / End
go to the beginning / end of the motion
.TP
.B O
toggle looping
.TP
.B Z
toggle the ground shadow
.TP
.B X
toggle the self shadow (also switched by the self shadow keys of the VMD)
.TP
.B L
toggle the VMD light motion (off: MMD default light)
.TP
.B R
reset the camera (front view framing the whole model)
.TP
.B Esc
quit
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B pmx \-\-render dance.mp4 \-s song.wav \-c camera.vmd miku.pmx dance.vmd
the whole dance with music as an H.264 video (1280x720, 30 fps)
.TP
.B pmx \-\-render frames/ \-\-range 300:449 \-\-size 1920x1080 \-\-fps 60 miku.pmx dance.vmd
five seconds as 300 PNG files frames/00000.png ... frames/00299.png
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/mikumikupenguin/shaders/
GLSL shaders (a \fIshaders/\fR directory in the current directory takes
precedence).
.TP
.I /usr/share/mikumikupenguin/textures/
shared toon textures toon01.bmp \- toon10.bmp.
.TP
.I /usr/share/mikumikupenguin/doc/README_JP.html
Japanese documentation.
